From 8f2a6e16ff2e399d7c517da7a6e7f3f7fbb188ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AI Pairing <ai-pairing@calimly.local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 08:16:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S1: Swagger foundation + full Auth/Tenants documentation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Wire IncludeXmlComments for Presentation, ApplicationLayer, and
  DomainLayer assemblies (GenerateDocumentationFile enabled on the
  latter two) — previously GenerateDocumentationFile was only set on
  the Presentation project and IncludeXmlComments was never called at
  all, so none of the existing <summary>/<param>/<response> XML docs
  reached Swagger UI regardless of how complete they were in source.
- Add OpenApiInfo (title/version/description).
- Add EnumSchemaDescriptionsFilter (ISchemaFilter): documents every
  enum's numeric wire value + member docs on its schema, since no
  JsonStringEnumConverter is registered anywhere (enums serialize as
  plain integers).
- Add ExamplesOperationFilter + ExampleCatalog + EndpointExampleSet
  (IOperationFilter, same hand-written-filter pattern as the existing
  AcceptLanguageHeaderOperationFilter — no new NuGet package):
  attaches named, multi-scenario request/response examples per
  action, keyed by (Controller, Action).
- Add Swagger/Examples/AuthExamples.cs and TenantExamples.cs: full
  named examples for all 12 Auth + Tenants endpoints, grounded in the
  actual AuthService/TenantService/*Errors code (exact codes,
  messages, categories).
- Correct AuthController/TenantsController XML docs and
  [ProducesResponseType] to distinguish the two different 401/403
  shapes in this codebase: the empty-body kind the auth middleware
  returns before an action runs, vs. the enveloped ApiResponse<T> kind
  a Result-based failure returns (e.g. Tenant.ActorNotResolved on
  SoftDelete). Some actions previously declared a typed envelope body
  for a response that is actually always empty at runtime.
- Fix a doc-comment drift on CurrentPrincipalResponse: documented a
  TenantId parameter that doesn't exist on the record.

Foundation (XML comments, enum filter, examples filter/catalog) now
applies to every controller; only Auth + Tenants have full example
content so far. Remaining controllers land in phases S2-S5 per the
agreed module grouping.
